Section 12-10 (Excerpt): Selected Definitions
floor area

**Last Amended:** 2/2/2011

"Floor area" is the sum of the gross areas of the several floors of a **building or other structure**, measured from the exterior faces of exterior walls or from the center lines of walls separating two **buildings**. In measuring **floor area**, the following spaces shall not be included:

(a) elevator or stair bulkheads, accessory water tanks or cooling towers, or mechanical equipment space occupying not more than one-third of the roof area;

(b) space, including stairways or corridors, below the level of the first **story** as herein defined;

(c) **cellar** space;

(d) open or enclosed **accessory** off-street parking spaces;

(e) space used for **accessory** off-street loading berths; and

(f) open **balconies**, **loggias**, **arcades**, **colonnades**, **porticos**, **open porches**, or similar open spaces.

